# Desktop parity harness (in progress)

Build the document helper and the UI-test binary first:

```sh
devenv shell -- bun run desktop.gpui.build-helper
devenv shell -- cargo build --locked --features ui-tests --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml --bin twyne-desktop
devenv shell -- bun run desktop.gpui.parity
# Or: devenv shell -- bun run desktop.gpui.parity --states quiet,writing
```

Outputs are disposable under `desktop/gpui/target/parity/`; each invocation replaces that directory. The browser uses a fresh context and native captures allocate isolated Xvfb displays and libraries. The report exits nonzero when any selected state has no verified comparison. RMSE is normalized to 0–1 and the AE percentage uses a 2% fuzz threshold.

This is an incomplete harness: Source drivers are only attempted for quiet, writing, and desk, and document equivalence has not yet been established for those states. Other states are explicitly recorded as unmapped. Therefore no pixel scores are currently claimed. The retained native panel fixtures need corresponding web-store seeding and each state needs a verified Source interaction and content check before it can be compared.

