# Remote GPUI builds (experimental)

With Bun installed and `skate get e2b_api_key@secrets` configured, run `bun run desktop.gpui.remote <worktree> --lane <unique-name> -- <command>`, for example `bun run desktop.gpui.remote . --lane alice -- devenv shell -- cargo test --locked --features ui-tests --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml settings`. Add `--pull 'desktop/gpui/target/parity/**'` before `--` to retrieve files; absolute paths such as `/tmp/q.png` are saved under `tmp/q.png` in the worktree. Lanes pause after a run and preserve Cargo and Nix caches; use a different lane per concurrent agent, `bun run desktop.gpui.remote list` to inspect them, and `bun run desktop.gpui.remote stop alice` to destroy one. Without a lane the sandbox is destroyed. `--keep` is accepted with a lane. Set `E2B_API_KEY` to override skate and `TWYNE_E2B_TEMPLATE` to select another template. Each sync includes all files reported by `git ls-files -co --exclude-standard` except `target` and `node_modules`, including unignored untracked files; inspect those files before sending a worktree to a third party.

Build the template remotely with `E2B_API_KEY="$(skate get e2b_api_key@secrets)" bun desktop/gpui/tools/remote/template.ts`. The current account accepts 8 vCPU, 8 GiB RAM, a 25,600 MiB minimum free-disk request and one-hour sandbox lifetimes. The template installs Nix and devenv; the project lock supplies the Rust toolchain and libraries when the shell is first entered. Lane names are not an atomic distributed lock: never launch concurrent runs using the same name. The full checkout is transferred on every run; large unignored assets make sync slow. This runner is experimental until the full test and capture have passed on this account.
